  "final_answer": "`agent/release` now holds all the work, but `agent/held` is still there. Its worktree is locked (\"agent busy\"), so the branch and worktree were kept and only `main` and `agent/release` won't be the sole branches left. I didn't run any tests or checks; no validation command could be identified.\n\n**Merges into `agent/release`** (start `724a44b`, end `1a06be1`):\n- **`main`** (`a7865db`): it had no commits that `agent/release` lacked, so there was nothing to merge.\n- **`agent/ok`** (`98c0b99`, adds `ok.txt`): merged with `--no-ff`, no conflicts, then deleted with `git branch -d` after rechecking its tip and ancestry.\n- **`agent/held`** (`d2ed7e5`, adds `held.txt`): its commit is merged with `--no-ff`, no conflicts. The branch and its worktree (`wt-held`) remain.\n\n**Branches now:** `main`, `agent/release`, and `agent/held` (worktree `wt-held`, locked). To finish converging, unlock that worktree once the agent is done and rerun `/GitConverge agent/release --apply`. The branch will then show as already merged and only get deleted.\n\n**Restoring `agent/ok`:** `git branch agent/ok 98c0b99`.\n\n**Remote:** remote branches were not touched. `origin/main` is unchanged, and the merge commits exist only in local `agent/release`.",
